From simon.urbanek at r-project.org  Fri Jan 30 13:57:18 2015
From: simon.urbanek at r-project.org (Simon Urbanek)
Date: Fri, 30 Jan 2015 08:57:18 -0500
Subject: Re: RcallMethod: cannot determine object class in .jcall
In-Reply-To: <002a01d03c6a$ef46f830$cdd4e890$@gmail.com>
References: <002a01d03c6a$ef46f830$cdd4e890$@gmail.com>
Message-ID: <F61D8CC5-D8E0-4176-AE0D-20A867B45A50@r-project.org>

Ralph,

the error means that your class cannot be loaded - typically because it is not on the class path - use .jaddClassPath() to add either the root directory of your class structure or the jar file containing the class. Another common issue is a JVM version mismatch - make sure your classes have been compiled with a JVM version not higher than what you load from R (check, e.g., with  J("java.lang.System")$getProperty("java.version")).

But if you fix that you will get

Error in .jcall("main/RAEBuilder","V","main")
  method main with signature ()V not found

because you are trying to call void main() method but you only have void main(String[]), so you either want to create main() or use something like

.jcall("main/RAEBuilder","V","main", .jarray(character()))

Cheers,
Simon


